---
import ServicePage from '../components/ServicePage.astro';
---

<ServicePage
  slug="data-enrichment-hygiene"
  title="Data Enrichment & Hygiene: Clean, Deduped, Compliant Data, Automatically"
  description="CRM data cleanup, deduplication, enrichment, and compliance so your team stops wasting hours on bad data and your reporting is finally trustworthy."
  serviceName="Data Enrichment & Hygiene"
  serviceTag="Data Enrichment & Hygiene"
  serviceSchemaDescription="CRM data cleanup, deduplication, enrichment, validation, and compliance, maintained with automated hygiene workflows so records stay clean over time."
  headlineParts={['Clean data.', 'Without the manual cleanup.']}
  subtitle="Deduped, enriched, compliant records, maintained automatically, so your team stops fixing data and your reports are finally trustworthy."
  hook="Dirty data quietly breaks everything downstream. Duplicates split a customer across three records, missing fields stop routing and reporting from working, and stale contacts waste outreach and ad spend. Most teams patch it by hand, which never scales and never stays fixed. The answer is not a one-time scrub. It is rules and automation that keep the data clean as it comes in, so nobody has to think about it again."
  whatsIncluded={[
    'Deduplication: merge rules that collapse split records without losing history',
    'Enrichment: fill in the firmographic and contact data your team and routing need',
    'Validation and normalization: consistent formats so filters, reports, and workflows hold',
    'Automated hygiene plus compliance: ongoing cleanup, consent, and suppression handling built in',
  ]}
  goodFitIf={[
    'Your CRM is full of duplicates and half-empty records nobody trusts',
    'Reps and reporting work around the data instead of relying on it',
    'Someone is spending hours on manual list cleanup, or you are worried about compliance',
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'What tools do you use for this?',
      htmlA: 'It depends on your stack. Enrichment often runs through Clay or native CRM tools; dedup and hygiene through HubSpot or Salesforce operations features plus automation in n8n or Zapier. I work in the tools you already have rather than adding another subscription where I can avoid it.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Is this a one-time cleanup or ongoing?',
      htmlA: 'Usually both. We start with a one-time pass to fix the backlog, then put rules and automation in place so new data stays clean. A one-time scrub without the automation just buys you a few months before the mess returns.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can you help with compliance and consent?',
      htmlA: 'Yes. Hygiene and compliance go together: suppression lists, consent tracking, and unsubscribe handling are part of keeping the database clean and keeping you out of trouble. I am not a lawyer, but I build the operational side so your data practices match your policy.',
    },
    {
      q: 'How much does data work cost?',
      htmlA: 'Pricing depends on scope and the size of the database. A one-time cleanup plus hygiene automation runs as a fixed-scope project. Ongoing data ownership runs as a retainer. See the <a href="/pricing" class="link-teal">engagement models</a>, then book a call so we can share a precise number against your situation.',
    },
  ]}
  relatedServices={[
    { slug: 'crm-implementation', title: 'CRM Implementation', sub: 'The system the clean data lives in' },
    { slug: 'process-automation', title: 'Workflows & Automation', sub: 'Keep data clean automatically' },
    { slug: 'reporting-analytics', title: 'Reporting & Analytics', sub: 'Reporting you can finally trust' },
  ]}
  ctaHeadline="Ready to trust your data again?"
  ctaBody="Book a free 30-minute call. No pitch, no proposal. An honest look at the state of your data and what it would take to fix it for good."
  heroImage="/images/hero-tech-stack-audit.jpg"
/>
